The '''Toong''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] of bipeds with a unique appearance that were [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Tund]]. They possessed long [[Limb|legs]] and arms, several skin [[color]]s, and a large head located where the torso would normally be in [[humanoid]]s. One famous Toong was [[Ben Quadinaros]], a [[Podracing|podracer]] who participated in the [[Boonta Eve Classic]].

==Biology and appearance==
The Toong were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] of bipeds with a unique appearance that were [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Tund]].<ref name="Alien Archive" /> Their natural habitat was [[forest]] or [[jungle]].<ref name="VE" /> They possessed long [[Limb|legs]] and arms, several skin [[color]]s, and a large head located where the torso would normally be in [[humanoid]]s. Their faces featured a tiny upturned [[nose]] and orange [[eye]]s. Three [[antenna]]e sprouted from the top of their skull.<ref name="DB" />

==Society and culture==
The Toong were known as an extremely timid race who preferred the company of their own families. Due to their nature, Toong avoided confrontations with the wider [[galaxy]]. Several Toong were able overcome their shyness and become racers.<ref name="Alien Archive" />

==Toong in the galaxy==
Several Toong were famous racers, including [[Lor Kelasakuroona]], a Toong [[racer]] who participated in the [[Forty-eighth annual Dragonfire Air Rally|forty-eighth]] annual [[Dragonfire Air Rally]] on [[Coruscant]],<ref name="Dooku: Jedi Lost script">[[Dooku: Jedi Lost (script)|''Dooku: Jedi Lost'' script]]</ref> and [[Ben Quadinaros]], a famous Toong [[Gender|male]] [[Podracing|podracer]], who claimed to have come from the mysterious [[Tund system]].<ref name="DB" /> During the [[Invasion of Naboo|Naboo Crisis]], Quadinaros participated in the [[Boonta Eve Classic]], though his [[podracer]] malfunctioned, and he never got past the starting line.<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> Despite his embarrassing loss, Quadinaros persisted in podracing and was billed as the racer [[Sebulba]]'s arch-nemesis on the poster ''[[The Sport's Greatest Rivalry]]'' during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Propaganda">''[[Star Wars Propaganda: A History of Persuasive Art in the Galaxy]]''</ref>

Also during the Clone Wars, various Toong worked under a [[Unidentified Trandoshan manager|Trandoshan manager]] at a [[Pyke Syndicate]] [[spice]] shipping dock on [[Oba Diah]]. [[Rafa Martez|Rafa]] and [[Trace Martez]] attempted to trick the workers into loading their [[Silver Angel|ship]] with spice by claiming they had a delivery order. One such [[Unidentified Toong worker|Toong worker]] called his [[Unidentified Trandoshan manager|Trandoshan manager]] for assistance, leading to a scuffle between the two groups.<ref name="Together Again" />

A [[Unidentified Toong vendor|Toong vendor]] sold ship parts in a [[Unidentified trading post (Rex Strata)|trading outpost]] on the planet [[Rex Strata]] during the [[High Republic Era]]. When two [[Youngling]]s, [[Inaya]] and [[Nash Durango]], approached the vendor, he refused to sell them parts until Inaya proved her abilities by repairing a starship component.<ref name="The Secret Ship">{{YJA|The Secret Ship}}</ref>

